This meta-user layer carries the ZCU102 fwTPM customizations for this
PetaLinux project. It is not a general-purpose Yocto layer.

Contents
========

- recipes-bsp/device-tree/files/system-user.dtsi
    Lock-step RPU + OpenAMP device tree: 1 MiB rproc_0_reserved carveout,
    vring/buffer regions and the ZynqMP IPI mailbox, QSPI disabled for
    Linux (owned by the R5 fwTPM), and ttc3 disabled so the R5 timer use
    does not collide with Linux timekeeping.

- recipes-bsp/fwtpm-r5/
    Stages the prebuilt Cortex-R5 firmware ELF (fwtpm_r5.elf) into
    /lib/firmware so Linux remoteproc can load it. The ELF is built under
    firmware/fwtpm-r5/ and staged with "make stage" (see the top-level
    petalinux/README.md).

- recipes-apps/fwtpm-rpmsg-test/
    Builds the /usr/bin/fwtpm_rpmsg_test OpenAMP RPMsg smoke-test client.

- recipes-kernel/linux/ (openamp.cfg)
    Enables remoteproc + RPMsg char + ZynqMP IPI mailbox kernel options.

See ../../README.md and ../../../README.md for build and usage details.
